# Dialogs & command palettes — unified surface

In ICARE-CVD frontend overlays (dialogs, search/command palettes, drawers):

- **Do not** separate header, body, and footer with `border-t`, `border-b`, or contrasting strip backgrounds (`bg-[#FAFAF8]` vs `bg-white`) when they belong to one card.
- Keep **one continuous white surface**; use spacing (`space-y-*`, `py-*`) instead of divider lines.
- For shadcn `CommandInput`, override the default wrapper border: `[&_[data-slot=command-input-wrapper]]:border-0` on the parent `Command`.

```tsx
// ❌ Wrong — visual “bands” inside one dialog
<CommandInput className="border-b border-[#E8E6E0]/80" />
<div className="border-t bg-[#FAFAF8]">Footer</div>

// ✅ Correct — single surface, spacing only
<Command className="[&_[data-slot=command-input-wrapper]]:border-0">
  <CommandInput className="border-0" />
</Command>
<div className="px-4 py-2.5">Footer</div>
```

Reference: `frontend/src/app/(doctor)/DoctorHeaderSearch.tsx`.
